\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::1>
\f2 Working chapter title: 
\f1\b \strokec2 If the Word Wasn\'92t Talking Matricide
\f2\b0 \strokec2 .\
This is a development guide, not a scene specification. The running order below proposes places to use the cutaways; it does not require all of them. Later prose takes precedence.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 What the sequence does\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 Alexander brings his mother before the entertainment machinery introduced in the first Candid Criminal scene. His evidence includes real wrongdoing, material extracted from Chip, and whatever his editing makes those things mean. His studio audience includes the muscle-necks who have transferred their allegiance from Eloise to him.\
The broadcast exposes that transfer of power. Beyond the auditorium, people interpret it according to their own knowledge, loyalties and purposes. Some act. The show\'92s conclusion prompts Major Midler to order the troops in.\
Eloise must survive, but the manner of her rescue remains open. Her release does not automatically restore the loyalty of the people who have enjoyed watching her trial.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Established material to carry in
\f0\b0\fs24 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Use the first Candid Criminal episode as the production template: greeting and audience responses; special guest; evidence package; interrogation; voting; sponsors; Wheel of Death; execution.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The first audience\'92s responses include \'93If you hadn\'92t done it, we wouldn\'92t have to vote!\'94, \'93Guilty!\'94, \'93Unanimous!\'94 and \'93we value the enthusiasm!\'94 Recognition gives these repetitions their force.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The evidence-package style is established: grainy, high-contrast, low-colour images, ending with the defendant\'92s magnified face. Apply the existing treatment to Eloise and Chip\'92s testimony.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The wheel is rigged. Shark tank is Alexander\'92s intended outcome. Eloise is strapped to her favourite Ermine Muller office chair.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The transported nativity figures are available for the Christmas staging. Their resemblance to Alexander and Sarah has already been established; their appearance need not be explained again.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Alexander is an adept manipulator and television professional despite his foolishness. His immediate justifications can change. Do not impose a consistent rescue mission or moral programme on him.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Chip supplied recorded material for manipulation. He is backstage, effectively constrained by Alexander\'92s insistence that he watch the show. He does not initially know the intended matricide.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Sarah, Hayley and Kathy are confined. Bala freeing them is a live option, not yet a completed event.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The audience\'92s muscle-necks are active supporters of Alexander. A moral objection does not automatically win this room back.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The preceding laboratory scene has already looked ahead to Quark discovering the GygesOS update. Its revised transition explicitly refers to this intervening broadcast. This sequence returns to Christmas Eve.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The early show establishes that surviving an execution can lead to another spin and another punishment. Equipment failure alone does not oblige Alexander to pardon Eloise.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

