\f1\b \cf0 8. Alexander\'92s ending
\f2\b0 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 He attempts to frame the result, complete the broadcast or escape. Eloise\'92s survival and his loss of control need not become clear to every viewer simultaneously.\cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Major Midler.
\f2\b0 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 What he sees at the conclusion prompts the order to advance. Finish this cutaway with the order or its immediate execution.\cell \lastrow\row
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 These slots can merge. In particular, the Sisters can recognise the guest and the altered testimony in one visit. The pub and High Elvis material can form one passage. Gerry and Jones can share one passage. There need not be a cutaway at every production transition.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 What each viewing thread needs\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2><$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 The Three Sisters\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f2 They have the richest knowledge of the accusations and the strongest personal reasons to disagree about the spectacle. Sarah has just used Alexander\'92s interest in her to ask for help. Hayley understands his methods. Kathy has her own history with Eloise and need not become a detached comic commentator.\
Use their differences selectively. All three do not need a response to every revelation. Their eventual action should emerge from the exchange, without a general debate on the ethics of capital punishment. Saving Eloise need not mean forgiving her or agreeing to resume her orders.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Bala\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f2 His contribution should be an action enabled by his practical role and access. If he frees the Sisters, that is already a consequential contribution. It need not be supplemented with another elaborate intervention in the execution apparatus.\
The old provisional rescue based on a fabricated maintenance regulation is dispensable. Do not make a live execution stop merely because he produces a certificate.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Major Midler\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f2 He is watching for consequences relevant to his operation. A brief earlier glimpse can establish that he recognises Eloise\'92s own employees in Alexander\'92s audience. Reserve his substantial response for the ending.\
Choose what the conclusion gives him: evidence of a command breakdown, a perceived opening, or another reason consistent with the eventual action. The broadcast is evidence he interprets, not necessarily an accurate account. His order does not itself establish that Shakti defences have stopped working.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Pub Elvi and the High Elvis\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f2 The pub offers music, food, drink and people waiting to perform. Use those existing activities to give the response a setting. The performers can dislike being delayed while remaining unable to stop watching.\
The High Elvis matters if his interpretation changes what others do. If he simply expresses another opinion, the ordinary Elvi may already do that work. His precise instruction, if any, remains to be decided; do not manufacture a new religious ruling merely to justify his inclusion.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Chanta\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f2 His cutaway needs a particular provocation and a decision. Alexander\'92s treatment of Eloise, possessive claims about Sarah, or an assertion of family authority can provide it. Chanta need not interpret the danger correctly in every respect.\
Retain his actual location and travel time. Concern during the broadcast does not require his immediate arrival at the auditorium. The earlier plan places his arrival on Christmas morning; changing that would affect the later convergence.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Gerry and Agent Jones\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f2 Gerry\'92s presence in the audience is proposed, not settled. If retained, it supplies an economical place to pay off his infiltration: he is already inside when we notice him. His attention can distinguish the show from the opportunity it creates.\
Jones is pursuing Jihad Man. He can observe a gesture, exchange or departure by Gerry and assign it conspiratorial meaning. His physical vantage needs to make that observation possible; it can be established briefly. He does not need to explain his whole theory again.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 The audience inside the auditorium\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 Keep its behaviour present through the show. These are people who have recently guarded Eloise and now enjoy condemning her. Their applause, familiarity with the format and readiness to obey Alexander make his authority tangible.\
They may approve different things: punishment of a domineering employer, humiliation of a powerful woman, celebrity access, or the prospect of seeing an execution. Choose individual responses where they sharpen the scene; do not pause for a catalogue of motives.\
Their allegiance makes a simple appeal to decency unreliable. An intervention can defeat the execution without converting the audience. The rescuers may leave with Eloise while the crowd remains furious at being deprived of its entertainment.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Rescue: choices still open\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 The rejected treatment is the conventional last-second interruption with Eloise\'92s feet just entering the water. Do not restore it under slightly different staging.\

