\f1\b \cf0 Rescue succeeds but the broadcast misrepresents the result
\f2\b0 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Different viewers act on different accounts; Alexander may salvage the appearance of success.\cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Decide precisely what the studio sees, what viewers see and what Midler believes. This choice has consequences beyond the scene.\cell \lastrow\row
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 Chip is a strong possible physical participant because he is present, capable and newly confronted with the use of his testimony. Sarah and Hayley can determine what happens to the rescued Eloise. Bala can make their involvement possible. These are available roles, not a requirement to give everybody part of the rescue.\
The chair should remain specific: Eloise\'92s favourite Ermine Muller, an object associated with her ordinary exercise of power. Its condition, handling or loss can contribute to the comedy without becoming an unprepared escape gadget.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

