\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Writing and pacing\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 Use the first show\'92s familiar beats to compress explanation. The new pleasure lies in who occupies its roles, what the footage does to known events, and how the audience responds to its former employer.\
Each cutaway should deliver a discovery, disagreement with consequences, decision or action. Return to a viewer when something has changed. Once rescue action is underway, let it run long enough to be understood.\
Carry the broadcast into a cutaway through something concrete\'97a question, image, vote or instruction. Return on a changed beat. A commercial break can accommodate action elsewhere, but repeated conveniently timed interruptions would become another formula.\
Do not replay the complete Kebab history in the evidence package. The reader has just heard Chip\'92s interview. Selected alterations can demonstrate Alexander\'92s manipulation more sharply than another full account.\
Keep the hour-long broadcast distinct from the reading time of the sequence. Its internal timing can be settled after the action is chosen. Any existing duration of 242 seconds is an unknown-duration placeholder, not a constraint.\
}